      then commit","body":"The thug keeps turning toward its target only while its
      attack telegraphs. When the telegraph closes it is committed: a target that
      steps aside is missed. The walk-in may time out; the turn is given back either
      way.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"046445ec-ef95-497a-ac1a-086ac3215f5e","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":300.0,"yMin":1060.0,"xMax":600.0,"yMax":1210.0},"title":"Still
      its turn?","body":"The director takes a token back when it is held too long,
      and the walk-in can be long. Asking again here means a thug that lost the turn
      on the way does not swing beside the one that has it now.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"50db7a26-3d41-4aae-af1c-452aa77c115c","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-900.0,"yMin":480.0,"xMax":-600.0,"yMax":630.0},"title":"One
      turn, one or more swings","body":"The director decides how many attacks a turn
      is worth when it grants the token (CombatConfig, encounter: min and max attacks
      per turn). Each swing spends one. After the last the director takes the token
      back, the guard on the swing refuses the next one, and Until Failure ends.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"e38892ea-21a5-48f5-bbf1-2a5001447b57","$type":"ArcaneOnyx.GraphCore.StickyNote"},{"VariableKind":"Graph","NodeComment":null,"relations":{"$content":[],"$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ConnectionCollection`3[[ArcaneOnyx.BehaviorTree.IPortRelation,
